ain:.4f}, Val AUC: {auc_val:.4f}\")\n    return model, training_loss, validation_loss, training_auc, validation_auc\n\ndef plot_and_save(metric_train, metric_val, metric_name, filename):\n    plt.figure()\n    plt.plot(metric_train, label=f'Training {metric_name}')\n    plt.plot(metric_val, label=f'Validation {metric_name}')\n    plt.title(f'{metric_name} per Epoch')\n    plt.xlabel('Epoch')\n    plt.ylabel(metric_name)\n    plt.legend()\n    plt.savefig(filename)\n    plt.close()\n\ndef main(dryrun=False):\n    X_train, Y_train, X_val, Y_val = load_data()\n    X_train, Y_train, X_val, Y_val = preprocess_data(X_train, Y_train, X_val, Y_val)\n    model = Classifier(input_dim=X_train.shape[1])\n    epochs = 1 if dryrun else 20\n\n    trained_model, training_loss, validation_loss, training_auc, validation_auc = train_model(\n        model, X_train, Y_train, X_val, Y_val, epochs=epochs)\n\n    model_filename = sys.argv[0].replace(\".py\", \"\") + \"_model.pth\"\n    torch.save(trained_model.state_dict(), model_filename)\n\n    plot_and_save(training_loss, validation_loss, \"Loss\", \"training_loss.png\")\n    plot_and_save(training_auc, validation_auc, \"AUC\", \"training_auc.png\")\n\n    print(\"Training complete. Outputs and model saved successfully.\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    dryrun = '--dryrun' in sys.argv\n    main(dryrun=dryrun)",
"explanation": "This Python code performs binary classification to distinguish four-top events from background processes using a deep neural network, with the goal of maximizing AUC.\n\nKey features:\n\n1. **Data Preprocessing:**\n   - Standardizes input features with `StandardScaler` to ensure faster and more stable training.\n   - Handles tensor conversion and dimensionality correctly.\n\n2. **Model Architecture:**\n   - A feedforward neural network with 3 hidden layers using `ReLU`, `BatchNorm1d`, and `Dropout` (regularization).\n   - Final layer uses `Sigmoid` for binary classification.\n   - Architecture allows learning complex patterns while reducing overfitting.\n\n3. **Training Loop:**\n   - Uses `Adam` optimizer and `BCELoss` on sigmoid output.\n   - Uses `roc_auc_score` to track AUC on training and validation sets each epoch.\n   - Uses PyTorch's `DataLoader` with batching and shuffling.\n\n4. **Evaluation & Plotting:**\n   - Tracks and plots both loss and AUC for training/validation.\n   - Saves plots and trained model.\n\n5. **Device Support:**\n   - Training leverages GPU if available.\n\nThis structure is designed with scientific accuracy and numerical performance in mind to give the highest possible AUC score using PyTorch."
}
