 metric\n\n**Why this approach maximizes AUC:**\n1. Feature engineering captures physics-based information that helps distinguish signal from background events.\n2. The deep architecture allows the model to learn complex patterns in the data.\n3. Regularization techniques (dropout, batch normalization, weight decay) prevent overfitting and improve generalization.\n4. Direct optimization of AUC through learning rate scheduling based on validation AUC.\n5. Batch processing allows efficient training on large datasets.\n\nThis approach combines domain knowledge from particle physics with modern deep learning techniques to create a robust classifier optimized for AUC performance on this four-top-quark classification task."
